  "acceptance": [
    "Canonical supported runtimebridge caps the complete HTTP envelope at 4MiB before JSON decoding, including event metadata and failure text; oversize Observe returns typed non-retryable invalid_response without a partial observation or response/credential echo.",
    "Actual HTTP valid JSON boundaries 4MiB-1, 4MiB, 4MiB+1 tested with padding in event kind rather than payload. Below/exact preserve complete event/cursor/payload; over refuses.",
    "External Go overlay disables only existing post response-size refusal; valid over-limit JSON is then admitted and owning new test fails exactly there (below/exact still pass). No repository production bytes were changed.",
    "Existing safe projection masks complete payload before16KiB truncation, bounds each payload4MiB/page16MiB, and omits oversize inputs without exposing an unmasked prefix.",
